  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "The one-cent errors came from floating-point math in `billing/totals.py`. `line_total_cents` used `float` for the price, quantity and tax. Values like `1.005` or `2.675` aren't exactly representable as floats, so they land just under the half-cent. Python's `round()` then rounds them down, and the line total comes out one cent low. Because the invoice total is the sum of the line totals, the error carries into the `TOTAL` row.\n\nI switched the calculation to `Decimal` and `ROUND_HALF_UP`, which is the rounding the README documents (\"rounded half up to the cent\"). `1.005` now gives 101 cents and `2.675` gives 268. The existing tests pass, but I didn't add a test for these half-cent cases.\n\nThe change is only in `billing/totals.py`. I didn't run the report on your actual CSV, so I haven't confirmed the affected rows are now correct.",
